+```
+
+The reported failure reproduced alone against the queue executable: the refinement-entry assertion failed after 10.65 seconds with an empty status. A second reproduction inspected only the task-owned test process's threads and file descriptors. Its refinement worker had the owner's `/home/zdavidson/Documents/AI Models/ComfyUI/models/diffusion_models/flux-2-klein-9b-fp8.safetensors` open. That file is 9,433,061,528 bytes. `refine::Checker::check_inner` resolves the selected preset filename against the configured local model directories, then `hash_file` reads and hashes the whole file before recipe testing. Thus this supposedly mock-only test depended on the owner's installed weights and could exhaust its ten-second deadline before submitting a mock prompt. This resolves the previously documented, pre-existing mock failure; the timeout was not the underlying defect.
+
+The fix stays in the failing UI test. It advertises uniquely named mock Klein 9B weights through the existing `MockComfy::set_model_dir` API, discovers them through the real inventory API, and selects that installed model before clicking Refine. The name includes the mock endpoint, so it cannot collide with the regular installed preset. The fixture lives under the test's disposable library root, and the existing reset guard also clears the test inventory. The actual refinement verifier, HTTP generation, result event dispatch, library save/load, Use with Undo, and Open as a new document all remain exercised. Failure diagnostics now include session jobs and the number of submitted prompts.
+
+Getting past the original timeout exposed a second test setup race at the previously unreachable Use assertion. A diagnostic run passed, but its immediate repeat failed: the completion-frame Use rectangle was `[[209.0 708.0] - [261.2 736.0]]`, then became `[[177.0 708.0] - [229.2 736.0]]` in the click frame. The pointer was sent to the old center (235.1), outside the new right edge (229.2), so the command never ran; the generated-success status remained unchanged. The result controls cause the modal to resize after completion. The test now renders three frames before querying and clicking those new controls, matching the existing library-action test's preparation. This waits for UI geometry rather than retrying a failed command. The exact undo-history assertion remains intact and now includes status and button geometry on failure.
+
+TEST-CHANGED: `draft_refine_mock_comfy_uses_source_and_library_results_can_be_used_or_opened` now selects mock-only weights from the same Klein model family instead of allowing its mock preset name to resolve to the owner's real weights, and settles the newly resized result UI for three frames before clicking. No existing expectation, assertion, or ten-second job deadline was removed or relaxed. Added assertions require the fixture's family to match Klein 9B and its exact filename to appear in the submitted graph. This changes test setup, not the expected application behavior.
